---
description: Memory, graph, and evolution layer rules
globs:
  - "memory/**/*.py"
  - "graph/**/*.py"
  - "evolution/**/*.py"
  - "backend/memory/**/*.py"
---

# Memory rules
- Vector memory stores semantic failure patterns and outcomes.
- Graph memory stores relationships and blast radius.
- Time-series storage tracks decisions and evolution cycles.
- Deduplicate near-identical records.
- Keep memory explainable and auditable.

# Graph rules
- Use clear node and edge types.
- Preserve timestamps and metadata.
- Keep traversal deterministic where possible.
- Do not store PII in embeddings.

# Evolution rules
- Human approval is required before applying updates.
- Weight changes must be explicit.
- Evolution reports must be human-readable.
